OpenSuperSampling (OSS)
=======================

Originally developed by Cash Conway (cashcon57@gmail.com).
Project home: https://github.com/cashcon57/open-supersampling
First public release tag: v0.5.0-pixel-temporal (2026-05-07).

Copyright 2026 Cash Conway and OSS contributors.

OSS is an open-source super-resolution and frame-extrapolation system for
games, built on a persistent 2D Gaussian canvas warped frame-to-frame by
exact engine motion vectors with covariance resampling at the rasterizer.
The architecture is documented in RESEARCH.md and the design memo at
docs/superpowers/experiments/2026-05-05-v6-architecture-canonical.md.

